  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">North Africa Migration and Development (NAMAD)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to enhance livelihood skills and strengthen protection for vulnerable migrants, while increasing social cohesion between migrants and receiving communities in Algeria, Egypt and Tunisia. Based on the needs in each country context, IOM&#x2019;s targeted interventions will address specific barriers and gaps by providing a range of skills development and training, providing protection support including shelter, mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS) and legal counselling, and organising social mixing activities to build trust and social cohesion.</narrative>
  </description>
